# Pairs with PeerAuthorityBounded. A missing seam passes instead of refusing, so a
# host without the membership seam elevates a restore onto any tree.
MODULE: PeerRestoreElevatesUnwiredSeams
TARGET: PeerAuthorityBounded
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: peer authority holds when the membership, options or topology seam is missing

--- FIND
HasPeerAuthority(c) == wired /\ c \notin {Self, NoCluster} /\ c \in topology
--- REPLACE
HasPeerAuthority(c) == c \notin {Self, NoCluster} /\ c \in topology
--- END
